---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import Waitlist from '../components/Waitlist.astro'
---

<Base
  title="Build 3 folders tonight"
  description="The free 3 folder start. Make them, name them, put one real file inside, and point your AI at it. About 20 minutes."
  path="/start"
>
  <section>
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <span class="badge badge--accent">Free, about 20 minutes</span>
      <h1>Build 3 folders tonight</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        This is the whole starting move. No install, no account, no tool you do
        not already have.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Make the folders</h2>
      <p>Anywhere you like. Your desktop is fine. Name them exactly this:</p>
      <pre class="tree"><b>01_research/</b>
<b>02_writing/</b>
<b>03_publishing/</b></pre>
      <p>
        The numbers matter. They are the order your work actually happens in,
        and they keep the folders sorted in that order everywhere you look at
        them.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Put 1 real file in 02</h2>
      <p>
        Call it <code>how-i-write.md</code>. Put your actual preferences in it.
        Not a prompt. Not instructions to an AI. Just the truth, as you would
        tell a new hire:
      </p>
      <pre class="tree"><i># How I write</i>

Short sentences
No exclamation marks
Never sound excited about software
Say the number or say I do not know</pre>
      <p>
        Yours will be different. That is the point. This file is worth more than
        any prompt you have ever pasted, because it stays.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Point your AI at it</h2>
      <p>
        Open whatever you use. Ask it for something you would normally ask for,
        and add 4 words:
      </p>
      <div class="callout">
        <p>
          Write me a post about pricing, <strong>using what is in 02</strong>
        </p>
      </div>
      <p>
        Same question you would have asked. Same model. Different answer,
        because it read the folder it was standing in.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Then keep going</h2>
      <p>
        Add a file to 01 about who your customers actually are. Add one to 03
        about where things get published and what you check first. Add an 04
        when you need it. Nothing you already built has to move.
      </p>

      <div class="callout">
        <p>
          <strong>If it does not work</strong>, the usual reason is the file is
          written to an AI instead of about you. Rewrite it as notes for a
          person and try again.
        </p>
      </div>

      <hr />

      <h2>When you want mine</h2>
      <p>
        I am putting my real setup, my actual folder structures, and my finished
        builds into a VIP classroom. It is not open yet. Leave your email and
        you will hear before anyone else.
      </p>
      <Waitlist id="start-waitlist" />
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
